  "content": {
    "id": "p16-q51-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "51",
    "prompt": "A polynomial in two variables $x$ and $y$ such as $x^3+x^2y+xy^2+y^3$, can be viewed as a polynomial in $x$, whose coefficients are polynomials in $y$. The same theorems and algorithms apply.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p16-q51-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Let $P(x)=x^3+x^2y+xy^2+y^3$. Find $P(y)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4y^3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nP(y)&=y^3+y^2y+yy^2+y^3\\\\\nP(y)&=4y^3.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q51-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use the division algorithm to find the quotient and remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $x-y$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Quotient $x^2+2xy+3y^2$; remainder $4y^3$.\n\nTreat $y$ as a coefficient when dividing in $x$.",
          "worked": "Treat $y$ as a coefficient. Long division gives\n$$\\begin{array}{r|rrrr}\n&&x^2&+2xy&+3y^2\\\\\\hline\nx-y&x^3&+x^2y&+xy^2&+y^3\\\\\n&-x^3&+x^2y&&\\\\\\hline\n&&2x^2y&+xy^2&+y^3\\\\\n&&-2x^2y&+2xy^2&\\\\\\hline\n&&&3xy^2&+y^3\\\\\n&&&-3xy^2&+3y^3\\\\\\hline\n&&&&4y^3\n\\end{array}$$\nThus\n$$P(x)=(x-y)(x^2+2xy+3y^2)+4y^3.$$\nThe quotient is $x^2+2xy+3y^2$ and the remainder is $4y^3$, agreeing with $P(y)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 140
      }
    ]
  },
